   269	  the extension to `c1, c3`, the second factor, the independent re-derivation and the connection to the
   270	  Li–Lou conjecture are not found in the sources read (NOVELTY-UNCLEAR).
   271	- C4 (classification in 𝒫, answer to Li–Lou's question (7)): not found in the sources read. Hietarinta's
   272	  mKdV- and sine-Gordon-type searches (1987, papers II–III) were not read; they treat different bilinear
   273	  pairs but could overlap (NOVELTY-UNCLEAR).
   274	- "Proved" is used only for C1, C2, Lemma 4.1–4.3 and Theorem 4.4 (three-soliton level). "Integrable" in
   275	  C3/C4 always means "passes the stated soliton test", never Lax or symmetry integrability.
